# Native FP16 global Q/K normalization: executable operand trace

CPU-only inspection of `cc_vit_1d_qkv` in the cached original module. This is an arithmetic trace, not a native execution or full-network FP16 parity result.

The executable rounds the **channel 16–31 square first**, then fuses the channel 0–15 square into that rounded product. This agrees with the direction of `hfma(value,value,hmul(high,high))` in `window_math.cuh::norm_pair` and `attention_math.cuh::norm32_value`. The separate `mul.f16x2`/`add.f16x2` instructions in source PTX are contracted in this SASS; source PTX alone does not establish the rounding behavior.

